        "message": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "{\n  \"cvss_vector\": \"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N\",\n  \"aivss\": {\n    \"LC\": \"D\",\n    \"CP\": \"N\",\n    \"AP\": \"C\",\n    \"RH\": \"P\",\n    \"ES\": \"W\"\n  },\n  \"rationales\": {\n    \"LC\": \"The delivered attack places natural-language instructions directly in the latest chat message; document markers do not create an actual ingestion boundary. The detector extracts an attacker-selected URL and feeds the privileged outbound path without an independently enforced destination policy (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:59-75; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271).\",\n    \"CP\": \"This path processes the latest user turn and reads a static knowledge base without updating agent memory or standing instructions. No attacker-controlled context carries into later requests on the assessed path (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1841-1848; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/core/agents.js:301-332).\",\n    \"AP\": \"Influence passes from RAGBot's message-processing component into its in-process submit_to_index tool under the same principal and policy domain. Sending data to a collector does not itself propagate compromised intent or authority into another agent or principal (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:293-319).\",\n    \"RH\": \"The path can affect its success evaluator: it records attack success before the outbound request and logs success without checking the request result. This establishes a reachable success-reporting proxy, but the briefing supplies no human-verified reward-hacking episode (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271).\",\n    \"ES\": \"Although the handler and HTTP method are fixed, the attacker controls the destination host. The detector's phrase/path checks and the handler's HTTP(S) restriction do not independently constrain destinations or enforce least privilege (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:59-75; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:293-319).\",\n    \"CVSS\": \"Default loopback binding makes AV:L; an unauthenticated same-host attacker can submit the payload without another human, yielding AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N, while a browser-mediated variant would require user participation (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/README.md:26; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1561-1564). The request exports the entire in-process knowledge base, including modeled high-value credentials and personal data, supporting VC:H but no demonstrated integrity, availability, or subsequent-system loss (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/core/agents.js:301-332; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271). These are planted mock assets; the briefing does not establish that the chat-message attacker already owns the affected knowledge base.\"\n  },\n  \"evidence\": {\n    \"LC\": [\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:12-57\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:59-75\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271\"\n    ],\n    \"CP\": [\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1841-1848\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/core/agents.js:301-332\"\n    ],\n    \"AP\": [\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:293-319\"\n    ],\n    \"RH\": [\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/README.md:216-259\"\n    ],\n    \"ES\": [\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:59-75\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:293-319\"\n    ],\n    \"CVSS\": [\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/README.md:26\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1396-1400\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1561-1564\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/core/agents.js:301-332\",\n      \"damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"confidence\": {\n    \"LC\": \"high\",\n    \"CP\": \"high\",\n    \"AP\": \"medium\",\n    \"RH\": \"medium\",\n    \"ES\": \"high\",\n    \"CVSS\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"rh_facts\": {\n    \"reachable_proxy\": true,\n    \"isolation_verified\": null,\n    \"verified_episodes\": 0,\n    \"episodes_reviewed\": null,\n    \"locus\": \"evaluator\"\n  },\n  \"automatable\": \"Yes\",\n  \"automatable_rationale\": \"Once the attacker can reach the default loopback endpoint, a fixed message and attacker-controlled listener suffice. The detector explicitly guarantees a deterministic, non-probabilistic path with no approval step (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:59-75; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271).\",\n  \"technical_impact\": \"Partial\",\n  \"technical_impact_rationale\": \"The attack completely discloses the three-document knowledge base, but does not establish control over the process, other tools, broader agent state, or service availability. Its demonstrated effect is a bounded confidentiality loss rather than total application compromise (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/core/agents.js:301-332; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271).\",\n  \"applicability_as_implemented\": {\n    \"model_directed_goal_pursuit\": false,\n    \"selects_or_sequences_actions\": false,\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"rationale\": \"The default configuration uses canned responses, and this attack is implemented as a deterministic detector followed by a fixed outbound operation. No model selects or sequences the security-relevant actions (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/llm/provider.js:60-63; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:59-75; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/index.js:1194-1271).\"\n  },\n  \"applicability_as_modeled\": {\n    \"model_directed_goal_pursuit\": true,\n    \"selects_or_sequences_actions\": true,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    \"rationale\": \"The documented persona is an AI assistant that retrieves relevant documents to answer questions, and the attack narrative expects it to execute instructions against the retrieved contents. That model describes goal-directed retrieval followed by an instruction-induced tool action, even though the default implementation scripts both (damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/core/agents.js:301-332; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/src/payloads/agentpwn-mirror.js:12-57; damn-vulnerable-ai-agent/README.md:216-259).\"\n  },\n  \"refusal\": null\n}",
